  "evidence": {
    "source.txt:L7-L7": "The added section 5.2 sentence explicitly places the alarmed indicator in the sodium hypochlorite bulk tank; LI_HYPO is its project alias. Its high-level alarm notifies operators; this indication does not automatically stop chemical unloading.",
    "source.txt:L3-L3": "HYPO_BULK is an outdoor tank receiving 12.5% sodium hypochlorite through unloading piping. The report describes a 6,500-gallon tank and atmospheric storage.",
    "source.txt:L6-L6": "For this model, H1 denotes the boundary-to-HYPO_BULK transfer, H2 the HYPO_BULK-to-HYPO_DAY transfer, H3 the HYPO_DAY-to-HYPO_PROCESS transfer, A1 the boundary-to-ACID_DAY transfer, and A2 the ACID_DAY-to-boundary transfer.",
    "source.txt:L4-L4": "Sodium hypochlorite is transferred from HYPO_BULK into HYPO_DAY, a smaller tank inside Mod B, and then from HYPO_DAY into HYPO_PROCESS, an otherwise unidentified process vessel.",
    "source.txt:L5-L5": "ACID_DAY is an outdoor day tank receiving 30% sulfuric acid in the unloading area. Its reported capacity is 8,500 gallons. Material goes from this tank directly into an unspecified process destination."
  }
